[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114095,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 110,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Carcinoma cuniculatum (CC) is a rare, well-differentiated, locally destructive, non-metastasizing squamous cell carcinoma type, characterized by a burrowing invasive pattern, keratin-containing crypts, and minimal cytological atypia.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:00:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114096,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 110,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8051/3 Carcinoma cuniculatum</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:00:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114097,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 110,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2B6E.0 Squamous cell carcinoma of other or ill-defined sites in the lip, oral cavity, or pharynx</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:00:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114098,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 110,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> epithelioma cuniculatum.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:00:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114099,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 110,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:00:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114100,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 110,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The gingivo-alveolar complex of the mandible is the commonest site, followed by that of the maxilla. The tongue, buccal mucosa, and lower lip are rarely affected {30607347}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:00:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114101,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 110,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Pain, swelling, mucosal ulceration, tooth mobility, and induration are common {30607347}. The presence of sequestra or yellow keratinaceous discharge from oral or cutaneous fistulae may lead to misdiagnosis as osteomyelitis or abscess {21862267; 24035112; 25443811}. Longstanding symptoms in some individuals may reflect diagnostic delay and/or the slow-growing nature of this tumour.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>On mucoperiosteal sites, CC presents radiologically as an osteolytic lesion with a poorly defined moth-eaten outline {30607347}. Sequestration may be evident {21862267}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:00:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114102,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 110,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>CC presents most commonly in the seventh and eight decades of life. There is no sex predilection.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:00:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114103,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 110,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:00:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114104,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 110,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The pathogenetic mechanisms are unknown, and there is no association with HPV {12424455; 19625845; 21643820}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:00:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114105,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 110,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>CC is predominantly endophytic with a white to yellow-white appearance. Infiltrative keratin-filled crypts may be seen.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:00:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114106,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 110,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "<p>CC is characterized by a primarily endophytic growth pattern of a burrowing labyrinthine network of well-differentiated squamous epithelium forming interconnecting keratin-filled crypts communicating with the surface. A minor exophytic component may be present. There is no more than mild nuclear atypia. Intraepithelial and stromal neutrophils are abundant, often with keratin microabscesses. Microsequestra are frequently associated with bone invasion.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>Non-representative sampling may lead to misdiagnosis as cystic well-differentiated squamous cell carcinoma, verrucous carcinoma, osteomyelitis, odontogenic keratocyst, orthokeratinized odontogenic cyst, or abscess {30607347}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-12-05T15:27:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114107,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 110,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:00:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114108,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 110,
        "headingId": 588,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:00:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 761,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 591,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114109,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 110,
        "headingId": 591,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> correlation with imaging; well-differentiated, heavily keratinizing squamous epithelium; mild atypia; a labyrinthine, burrowing, cohesive invasive pattern.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> keratin microabscesses; stromal neutrophils; microsequestra; bone invasion at mucoperiosteal sites.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:00:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 759,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 589,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114110,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 110,
        "headingId": 589,
        "headingText": "<p >Staging follows the eighth edition of the Union for International Cancer Control (UICC)&nbsp;/ American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) TNM staging system.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-07T12:42:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 760,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 590,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114111,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 110,
        "headingId": 590,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The prognosis is excellent after complete excision. Local recurrence is uncommon after correct preoperative diagnosis, and no metastases develop despite multiple interventions {30607347}. There are no known predictive factors.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T15:00:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]